From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Downstream Patch Queue <downstream@localhost>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Publish widget quota over collector leases

Extend control v2 widget leases with opt-in quota provider selection.
Schedule the existing supplier workers under persisted refresh deadlines and
send bounded, current quota projections with the same lease, without coupling
quota HTTP failures or cadence to statistics.

---
diff --git a/docs/shared-collector.md b/docs/shared-collector.md
index 8a752753..89244cde 100644
--- a/docs/shared-collector.md
+++ b/docs/shared-collector.md
@@ -185,3 +185,26 @@ This is an unpublished source/queue feature. Production ELF and fixed-loopback T
 only the former may be delivered as a collector asset. Local process/TLS checks do not validate App Attest,
 WidgetKit entitlement/signing, APNs acceptance or actual iPhone timeline delivery.
 
+## Widget quota feed
+
+Collectors advertising `widget_quota_v1` on control v2 accept optional
+`quotaProviders` on `widget_subscribe`: a set of up to four unique IDs from
+`codex`, `opencode-go`, `kimi`, and `commandcode`. Omission or an empty set
+disables quota publication. A new request ID can change the set on the same
+lease without resetting statistics confirmation or pacing.
+
+Confirmed, unexpired leases allow the existing quota service to schedule its
+provider workers once a minute. Workers honor their persisted refresh deadlines
+and preserve the original observation time on transient failures. Each widget
+receives only its selected providers' current readings, not account history.
+
+Quota uses the same bearer lease but independent HTTPS transport:
+`POST https://agent-speed.yooztech.com/v1/widget-quota-publish` with
+`{"quota":{"version":1,"hostId":hostId,"sampledAt":unixMillis,"records":[...]}}`.
+Each record contains `provider`, `recordKey`, and `snapshot`; `recordKey` is
+unpadded base64url of SHA-256 over the provider ID, LF, and opaque account ID
+(or the empty string). `sampledAt` is the increasing publication version;
+`snapshot.observedAt` remains nullable and represents the actual reading time.
+No SSH endpoint, provider credential, or supplier account label is included.
+Changed projections are sent at most once a minute across the collector. Quota
+HTTP failures do not change statistics publishing or lease authorization.
